hello everyone my name  is bradley today i'd like to talk to you  about all the incriminating evidence  that hackers  and other cyber criminals leave behind  so look what do you imagine when you  hear the words hacker or cybercriminal  do you envision some kind of reclusive  genius who hasn't gotten up from his  keyboard in maybe 20 years  perhaps you imagine someone who can get  their hands on anything in the digital  world  or perhaps someone that can read any  message break into any device or  steal money from any bank in the world  well  that's the image that's often given off  by hollywood films and sensational news  articles  what's left out of the picture is how  hackers ultimately get caught by law  enforcement  [Music]  and that's exactly what i want to dig  into today  so back in 2012 wormer was a well-known  figure  among both hackers as well as the  conventional i.t community  the anonymous affiliated hacker managed  to break into several government  computer systems  notably he broke into the new york  police department's computer system  now a year prior to this the nypd had  violently cracked down on occupy wall  street protesters now many of those  officers used violent tactics such as  using batons and pepper spray  and many had even covered their badges  so as to conceal their real identities  now thanks to wurma the identities of  those very officers were made public and  obviously many applauded  werma for this act but others were  really outraged wemma definitely took a  liking to all of this attention he was  getting  just like zorro he would leave traces of  himself at the scene of a hack  including a word that was instantly  recognizable to anyone who had surfed  the web 10 years ago  pawned but burma also had a habit of  leaving funny pictures behind  and one of those pictures ultimately led  to his downfall this  is the very picture i'm talking about  now is there anything here that you  think would give him away  well to answer this question you don't  actually need to look at the actual  picture  but rather the file itself starting in  the early 2000s  digital images began to contain what's  called exif data  now in short an exif is a type of text  that contains the main parameters of any  given photograph  which can include the make and the model  of the camera the shutter speed the iso  and so on but this information alone  would really not have been enough to  catch wormer  except for one important detail photo  was taken by wurma's fiancee  specifically on her brand new iphone and  unlike a regular camera an iphone has a  gps chip  which recorded the exact location at  which this photo was taken  nowadays many of us know that our  iphones constantly track where we are  but back in 2012 this was still  relatively new technology  so the police were actually able to use  this picture's exit data to pinpoint a  small house in the suburbs of melbourne  australia and there they found a woman  who quickly admitted that her boyfriend  had actually asked her to take the  picture and to no surprise this  boyfriend turned out to be wermer  himself now soon enough the police were  able to figure out where his true  identity he was a 30 year old software  engineer living in texas by the name of  figenio akoa  and they also got hold of his social  media accounts too including his  facebook messages  his at ananwama twitter handle and  in all these there was plenty of  incriminating evidence  woman was pretty quick to admit his  guilt and he was eventually found guilty  and imprisoned  although he was released in 2015 from  prison we're actually had to deal with a  less common form of punishment  which is actually being banned from the  internet  so if he wants to for instance watch a  netflix documentary about himself  well he'd have to ask his wife to do the  clicking for him  nowadays many websites use exif data  facebook use it to make maps of all your  travels  google readily admits that images with  exif data are prioritized by a search  engine  because of this whenever you upload  images of yourself online  be aware that hackers can actually use  the exif data within your photograph to  track you down  so look how do we fight back against  this  well for starters you can actually  prohibit your phone camera from  accessing your location data  this is one of the more simple solutions  but be aware that if you do happen to  update your device your camera  could go back to default and collect  your location data so  while i thoroughly recommend this method  it may not guarantee  full anonymity all of the time my next  recommendation is to manually check the  exif data of all of the photos you  upload  you may wish to change or delete  whatever data within the photo you're  not comfortable with sharing  now for this you'd actually need to  install specific software on your  computer  you might need to download an app on  your phone or even use a service that  specializes in just this on the other  hand there are some benefits to exif  data which you might not have considered  for instance you could locate a stolen  phone or a camera this way just by  looking at the photos  and there are actually services that can  help you with that by scouring the net  for photos that are taken with the  stolen device  now if you want to find out how much  information is stored in just one  photograph  you can do this yourself just simply  upload a file onto the exifer.net and  click  exit me  i'd now like to welcome to the stage a  man by the name of jeremy hammond  he's the founder of hackthissite.org and  he's well known for a pretty  schoolboy era he made back in 2012. now  jeremy hacked into the private  intelligence firm stratfor  as a result thousands of military  documents were leaked onto the internet  detailing a wide range of different  sensitive government secrets now you'd  think that jeremy being an experienced  hacker wouldn't leave much of a trace  right  well while the fbi was able to track him  down they weren't able to gather much  from his computer because his hard drive  was so well encrypted  plus you'd probably expect that hammond  wasn't very keen on showing his password  which you can imagine would have been  tens of digits long right  so very well could have been that  hammond got away scot-free  if it hadn't been for one small detail  jeremy  really liked his cat so much so that his  password  was in fact the name of his cat and just  to make that password  much more difficult to crack he threw in  a few numbers  at the end well one two three so  the password used by a man who hacked  confidential government secrets was um  chewy123  now unsurprisingly this wasn't too  difficult for investigators to figure  out  and needless to say the technical  experts at the fbi couldn't believe how  easy it was to guess  to achieve this you need some top of the  line equipment now when it comes to  password guessing some of you may have  heard of the brute force method  which involves guessing every possible  combination of letters and numbers  now this of course is no easy task so if  someone wants to guess your password  they'll have to try a combination of  commonly used passwords first and  well if that doesn't work then they'll  answer information about you  including what you do what you like who  you know and so on  then maybe adding a few common numbers  at the end and using these keywords  someone can try and guess your password  so if you're a huge football fan  i wouldn't recommend using the password  ronaldo one  but this method actually landed one of  the most infamous hackers  in the world in prison i want to pay my  respects to the comrades lockdown doing  hard time but staying strong  and show my appreciation for the abcs  the bookstore prisoners the certain days  calendar  those who wrote letters those who  visited those who attended court dates  i appreciate you unfortunately millions  of us use similarly  weak passwords so please do check if any  of your passwords are the names of your  relatives or pets or  maybe even your favorite sports team and  so on if so  then you're on very thin ice  but even the best be it a long or  randomized password doesn't necessarily  guarantee  full security the creator of the largest  drug selling website  learned this from his own experience  ross william albrecht  known as the dead pirate roberts was  very cautious when it came to security  and of course the password on his  computer well  that he used to control the silk road  was so strong  that it was almost impossible to guess  now  fbi agents in charge of this arrest  understood this perfectly well  therefore they developed a dramatic  takedown operation  they actually staged a fight between  visitors in the public library of san  francisco  warbricht was working on his website  ulbrich turned away from his laptop to  see what was happening understandably so  and as soon as he did  another agent grabbed the open computer  now almost at once all of the secrets  of the main darknet based drug lord  literally ended up in the hands of the  fbi  i hope you don't do any shady business  but i still wouldn't recommend  leaving your computer unattended open in  a public library  i mean in the end logging out of your  account just takes a couple of taps on  your keyboard right  i hope that i was able to illustrate how  simple mistakes can have enormous  consequences for your online safety so  make sure that you pay attention to how  you keep your data safe whether it's  the passwords that you're putting into  certain sites or even  the metadata included in certain images  because as you've seen even the most  clever  of hackers have made tiny errors that  have turned their lives completely  upside down you're watching some sub my  name is bradley and as always it's been  a pleasure  also don't be like jeremy hammond don't  use your cat's name as a password with  one two three stuck on the end